# The saved pages under scripts/lib/sources/fixtures are evidence: they are what
# learn.microsoft.com and aws.amazon.com served, byte for byte, and the parser
# tests mutate exact markup inside them. core.autocrlf would rewrite their line
# endings on checkout, which changes the bytes and breaks those tests on a
# fresh clone. Leave them alone.
#
# It matters more for the AWS pages than for the Microsoft ones. An AWS page
# carries its whole record as a single line of JSON inside a script tag, and a
# CRLF injected anywhere in that line is a parse error rather than a cosmetic
# difference: the fixture would stop being a page at all.
scripts/lib/sources/fixtures/*.html -text
